From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elkir0 <elkir0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] misc: modem_v1: the 3.10 link PM state machine behind
 pm_mode=fsm

With the locked-on PM of the port, AP2CP_WAKEUP and AP2CP_STATUS stay high
for as long as the CP runs, so the CP can never release the MIPI-LLI link
and sleep: a powered SS333 costs about 155 mW with the screen off, radio
on or off.  Port the 3.10 state machine (link_device_pm.c, modem_pm.h):
stock's states, transitions, 100 ms CP_HOLD_TIME and 500 ms watchdogs, with
GPIO descriptors written through the allow_hw gate, timer_setup(), an
unbound high-priority workqueue and the port's wakeup sources.  The CP2AP
interrupts stay the locked-on PM's edge-both, storm-guarded handlers; they
give the line's level to the state machine.

pm_mode selects the PM for each CP session at PHONE_START: lockon, the
default, is unchanged; fsm is the state machine.  It may be written only
while the CP is OFFLINE, so a boot always starts in lockon unless the
module is loaded with pm_mode=fsm.  debugfs ss333/status shows the mode,
the state, and counters of every state, hold, bark and failure.

Additions to stock, where its state machine waits for ever or misreads:
 - an LLI unmount handled before the CP2AP_STATUS low edge, in CP_FREE or
   ACTIVATING, takes the machine down as UNMOUNTING's does: stock dropped
   it there, then waited in UNMOUNTING for an unmount already gone, and the
   watchdog ended the CP session (seen once in about a hundred cycles);
 - ACTIVATING -> UNMOUNTING arms the UNMOUNTING watchdog;
 - a send that waits 5 s for the link ends the CP session (a mount that
   failed after CP2AP_STATUS rose, an unmount nobody asked for);
 - a CP2AP storm ends the session, and a session whose CP2AP interrupts are
   not live at PHONE_START stays locked on;
 - the fail handlers act only on a CP that is ONLINE or BOOTING, not during
   the power-off's wait for PHONE_ACTIVE nor on a CP already crashed;
 - stop_link_pm() cancels the watchdog and the CP_FREE work and releases the
   wake lock.

Passed on the tablet on 2026-11-05, CP online, no SIM, modules loaded by
hand into the daily kernel: lockon behaves as before; under fsm the CP
releases and remounts the link by itself, with all four lines low at rest,
20 of 20 sends woke an unmounted link from the AP side (HOLDING), 30 minutes
of soak and 10 CP power-offs in UNMOUNTED, CP_FREE and ACTIVE ran without a
watchdog or a failure.  A userspace replay of the state machine passes 361
checks.  Not yet measured: the power saved.  Not tested: calls, SMS and
data with a SIM.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
